 to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\n\r\nAdded a subset of texture shader functions with an offset.\r\n\r\nI think this is useful addition - user may use them to easy gather neighbor pixels (usually in range of 16 pixels (-8..7) by each axis) from a texture, without complex calculation on the UV-coord. The PR is more complex than expected, since the limit of the texel offset needs to be gathered from a Rendering Device. As noticed in GLSL documentation these functions cannot be used on cubemaps.\r\n\r\nImplemented:\r\n\r\n- [x] textureOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] textureLodOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureLodOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] textureProjOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureProjOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] textureProjGradOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureProjGradOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] textureProjLodOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureProjLodOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] textureGradOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureGradOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] textureGatherOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/textureGatherOffset.xhtml\r\n- [x] texelFetchOffset - https://registry.khronos.org/OpenGL-Refpages/gl4/html/texelFetchOffset.xhtml","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"a